From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:48:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/13] kboot: admit T8132 boards per handoff path from one
 table

aura f1b99783 (#149) hands the AOP over on the J604 as on the J713, by
naming both boards in dt_set_t8132_aop(). Three T8132 handoff paths are
still qualified per board: the AOP, the external DCP enable and SIO. A
check written out in each of them drifts, as the J604 AOP showed.

Add src/t8132_board.h: the T8132 boards admitted on each of those paths,
J713 and J604. The AOP gate reads it; it admits exactly what f1b99783
admits (J713 and J604), and the later dcpext and SIO changes read the
same table. Every admitted path still checks its live ADT values at boot
and refuses on a mismatch; another M4 board is skipped as before. The
J604 values the AOP path reads (the AOP DART's instance table, DAPF bank
and windows, and the AOP's firmware segments) match the J713's in the
J604's 26B123 template ADT; its iop-aop-nub aop-target (0, J713 1) is
not read by this path.

tests: test_t8132_board_admission checks the table (J713 every path but
the dcpext enable, J604 every path, look-alike names and other boards
none); test_t8132_aop_handoff_gate runs dt_set_t8132_aop() and
dt_set_aop_firmware() cut out of src/kboot.c for the J604, the J713 and
the J715.

Assisted-by: LLM
